
> **Note:** All subcommands require **Administrator permissions** or **Bot Owner** permissions.

---

## ⚙️ `/registration config-roles`
Configure or update the R1–R5 rank roles.

### Options
| Option | Description              |
|--------|--------------------------|
| `r1` | Role to assign for rank R1 |
| `r2` | Role to assign for rank R2 |
| `r3` | Role to assign for rank R3 |
| `r4` | Role to assign for rank R4 |
| `r5` | Role to assign for rank R5 |

### Example
  /registration config-roles r1:@Civilian r2:@Cadet r3:@Officer

## ⚠️ `/registration config-approval`
Set whether a rank requires manual approval (e.g., R4 & R5).

### Options
| Option | Description                                   |
|--------|-----------------------------------------------|
| `rank` (R1–R5) | Which rank’s approval rule to update  |
| `required` (true/false) | Whether approval is required |

### Example
  /registration config-approval rank:R4 required:true

## ➕ `/registration config-approver-add`
Add a role that is allowed to approve pending registration requests.

### Options
| Option | Description                                      |
|--------|--------------------------------------------------|
| `role` | Role granted permission to approve registrations |

### Example
  /registration config-approver-add role:@Moderators

## ➖ `/registration config-approver-remove`
Remove a role from the approver list.

### Options
| Option | Description                              |
|--------|------------------------------------------|
| `role` | Role to remove from approval permissions |

### Example
/registration config-approver-remove role:@Trial-Mod

## 📋 `/registration config-show`
Displays the entire current registration configuration:

- R1–R5 rank roles  
- Approval requirements per rank  
- Approver roles  
- Registration logging channel  

Use this to verify that your registration system is configured correctly.

---

## 🛰️ `/registration config-logchannel`
Set the channel where registration logs will be sent.

Logs include:
- Approved registrations  
- Denied registrations  
- Workflow errors  
- Debug messages for registration module  

### Options
| Option | Description                        |
|--------|------------------------------------|
| `channel` | Channel to send log messages to |

### Example
  /registration config-logchannel channel:#registration-logs

